{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793813081,"nonce":"GQf6H8givKmAQFKp6XVNW2CA58c=","title":"Typing after a fresh viewport rebuild updates the bound greeting but leaves the input showing its placeholder. Reproduced in the worker-backed catalog in isolated Chrome after warming Preview and switching to Live, and in a native headless test after fresh tree builds. A theme change could temporarily hide the problem.","message":"TextInput revision and focus Signals were first created under the widget build owner and disposed when that tree was replaced. The local fix creates them alongside TextInputData and keeps explicit widget-mounted readiness for deferred focus.\n\nLocal implementation: crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input/{data,edit,focus,widget}.rs. The recording regression rebuilds the viewport three times and verifies visible field pixels follow edits; four deferred-focus unit regressions pass. Actual Chrome tests at DPR1 and DPR2 verify one text event per character, field pixels, callbacks, viewport resizing and theme-family/scheme changes while preserving worker/canvas and input value.\n\nUncommitted; keep open for review. TextArea has a similar lazy revision pattern that has not been reproduced or changed here and should be audited separately.","files":null}]}